#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030eb6c4-5959-5e6a-9113-2a03b28b0205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721874} {:answer/id #uuid "11fc11d1-ea07-521b-82fa-7859c3c32c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721876} {:answer/id #uuid "1d332ffc-29ca-5682-b7d7-a16883b93bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721877} {:answer/id #uuid "4785da51-51d9-5aa2-bc78-3935ceba2423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721885} {:answer/id #uuid "f3193296-a7b2-5ffb-974b-68b395ac58ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721899}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721877} :answer-field/id #uuid "2edb074d-aeb2-5355-a335-d68201c27332" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0ba8d7f7-8d60-53dd-ba78-2aca5a659c0e" :question/problem "The path $C$ is the line segment from $A(-2,1)$ to $B(0,-1)$, traversed from $A$ to $B$. Evaluate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(- x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the endpoint parametrization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{r}(t)&=\\mathbf{a}+t(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\\n&=\\langle -2,1\\rangle+t\\langle 2,-2\\rangle \\\\\n&=\\langle 2 t - 2,1 - 2 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $x(t)=2 t - 2$, $y(t)=1 - 2 t$, and $\\mathbf{r}'(t)=\\langle 2,-2\\rangle$. Thus $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}t$ and $\\mathrm{d}y=-2\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nWrite $P(x,y)=- x y$ and $Q(x,y)=x$. Evaluate $P$ and $Q$ along the segment and retain their corresponding signed differentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP\\,x'(t)&=\\left(-1\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 t - 2\\right)\\cdot \\left(1 - 2 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right) \\\\\n&=8 t^{2} - 12 t + 4, \\\\\nQ\\,y'(t)&=\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 t - 2\\right)\\cdot \\left(-2\\right) \\\\\n&=4 - 4 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ denote the requested integral. Using the power rule gives an antiderivative $F(t)$ and the endpoint evaluation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(P\\,x'(t)+Q\\,y'(t)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(8 t^{2} - 16 t + 8\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{8 t^{3}}{3} - 8 t^{2} + 8 t\\right]_{0}^{1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(t)&=\\frac{8 t^{3}}{3} - 8 t^{2} + 8 t, \\\\\nF(1)&=\\frac{8 \\left(1\\right)^{3}}{3} - 8 \\left(1\\right)^{2} + 8 \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{8}{3}, \\\\\nF(0)&=\\frac{8 \\left(0\\right)^{3}}{3} - 8 \\left(0\\right)^{2} + 8 \\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=F(1)-F(0) \\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{8}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "302f5a16-2206-56ef-9084-d1af6f839fb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721881} {:answer/id #uuid "5dcf11ba-d1d5-53a8-9eed-55293025d5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721886} {:answer/id #uuid "cd276d8d-e818-5383-8e3d-a31f547e816d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721896} {:answer/id #uuid "d7677f6a-f934-58c1-bd42-1b1fe1fac23e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721897} {:answer/id #uuid "f13826f7-57cd-5c9c-8a72-71998901708c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721898}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721886} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcb07dd7-6457-5feb-8c68-a7b72ab39e9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2ad33ff1-b0f6-5687-88b0-fe80e662e635" :question/problem "The path $C$ is the line segment from $A(0,0)$ to $B(-1,-1)$, traversed from $A$ to $B$. Evaluate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the endpoint parametrization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{r}(t)&=\\mathbf{a}+t(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\\n&=\\langle 0,0\\rangle+t\\langle -1,-1\\rangle \\\\\n&=\\langle - t,- t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $x(t)=- t$, $y(t)=- t$, and $\\mathbf{r}'(t)=\\langle -1,-1\\rangle$. Thus $\\mathrm{d}x=-1\\,\\mathrm{d}t$ and $\\mathrm{d}y=-1\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nWrite $P(x,y)=x y$ and $Q(x,y)=1$. Evaluate $P$ and $Q$ along the segment and retain their corresponding signed differentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP\\,x'(t)&=\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(- t\\right)\\cdot \\left(- t\\right)\\cdot \\left(-1\\right) \\\\\n&=- t^{2}, \\\\\nQ\\,y'(t)&=\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(-1\\right) \\\\\n&=-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ denote the requested integral. Using the power rule gives an antiderivative $F(t)$ and the endpoint evaluation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(P\\,x'(t)+Q\\,y'(t)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- t^{2} - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=\\left[- \\frac{t^{3}}{3} - t\\right]_{0}^{1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(t)&=- \\frac{t^{3}}{3} - t, \\\\\nF(1)&=- \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{4}{3}, \\\\\nF(0)&=- \\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=F(1)-F(0) \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{4}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{4}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25dc5413-4f81-5d68-a7e2-7464a33434a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721878} {:answer/id #uuid "341ba1d2-ea6a-503b-a255-8942a10be262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721882} {:answer/id #uuid "69fd950c-5a45-5736-b7cb-7ef36f12af16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721890} {:answer/id #uuid "7c149774-51a9-59a5-8836-492011022251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721891} {:answer/id #uuid "a4976d42-07e9-5bfa-b66f-6c1a5a5ba571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721894}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721891} :answer-field/id #uuid "373c7dc2-c5d3-519d-a510-cf3505d1580b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b178e8ac-f7e0-5468-bf7a-8a83f4332418" :question/problem "The path $C$ is the line segment from $A(0,1)$ to $B(-1,-1)$, traversed from $A$ to $B$. Evaluate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(- x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the endpoint parametrization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{r}(t)&=\\mathbf{a}+t(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\\n&=\\langle 0,1\\rangle+t\\langle -1,-2\\rangle \\\\\n&=\\langle - t,1 - 2 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $x(t)=- t$, $y(t)=1 - 2 t$, and $\\mathbf{r}'(t)=\\langle -1,-2\\rangle$. Thus $\\mathrm{d}x=-1\\,\\mathrm{d}t$ and $\\mathrm{d}y=-2\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nWrite $P(x,y)=- x y$ and $Q(x,y)=1$. Evaluate $P$ and $Q$ along the segment and retain their corresponding signed differentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP\\,x'(t)&=\\left(-1\\right)\\cdot \\left(- t\\right)\\cdot \\left(1 - 2 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(-1\\right) \\\\\n&=2 t^{2} - t, \\\\\nQ\\,y'(t)&=\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(-2\\right) \\\\\n&=-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ denote the requested integral. Using the power rule gives an antiderivative $F(t)$ and the endpoint evaluation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(P\\,x'(t)+Q\\,y'(t)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t^{2} - t - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{2 t^{3}}{3} - \\frac{t^{2}}{2} - 2 t\\right]_{0}^{1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(t)&=\\frac{2 t^{3}}{3} - \\frac{t^{2}}{2} - 2 t, \\\\\nF(1)&=\\frac{2 \\left(1\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2} - 2 \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{11}{6}, \\\\\nF(0)&=\\frac{2 \\left(0\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2} - 2 \\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=F(1)-F(0) \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{11}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{11}{6}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b3b1c54-f8f0-53cd-81c0-b68ce9165bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{19}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721884} {:answer/id #uuid "61d93cce-a781-59c8-9bdc-a37613f9f8fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721887} {:answer/id #uuid "63878fa3-ca00-509b-8a83-d2b409a96f0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721888} {:answer/id #uuid "63b0a0b2-ad6a-5304-ad9d-4080cf04e4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721889} {:answer/id #uuid "8a11cde5-cfbe-5595-a2ca-5b2d229c6bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721892}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721888} :answer-field/id #uuid "a23f1efe-2a84-564f-8cfd-0725820a9b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fece0be0-7c68-58c1-8241-fad994b43f9b" :question/problem "The path $C$ is the line segment from $A(1,-1)$ to $B(2,-3)$, traversed from $A$ to $B$. Evaluate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the endpoint parametrization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{r}(t)&=\\mathbf{a}+t(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\\n&=\\langle 1,-1\\rangle+t\\langle 1,-2\\rangle \\\\\n&=\\langle t + 1,- 2 t - 1\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $x(t)=t + 1$, $y(t)=- 2 t - 1$, and $\\mathbf{r}'(t)=\\langle 1,-2\\rangle$. Thus $\\mathrm{d}x=1\\,\\mathrm{d}t$ and $\\mathrm{d}y=-2\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nWrite $P(x,y)=1$ and $Q(x,y)=- x y$. Evaluate $P$ and $Q$ along the segment and retain their corresponding signed differentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP\\,x'(t)&=\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=1, \\\\\nQ\\,y'(t)&=\\left(-1\\right)\\cdot \\left(t + 1\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\cdot \\left(-2\\right) \\\\\n&=- 4 t^{2} - 6 t - 2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ denote the requested integral. Using the power rule gives an antiderivative $F(t)$ and the endpoint evaluation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(P\\,x'(t)+Q\\,y'(t)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 4 t^{2} - 6 t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=\\left[- \\frac{4 t^{3}}{3} - 3 t^{2} - t\\right]_{0}^{1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(t)&=- \\frac{4 t^{3}}{3} - 3 t^{2} - t, \\\\\nF(1)&=- \\frac{4 \\left(1\\right)^{3}}{3} - 3 \\left(1\\right)^{2} - \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{16}{3}, \\\\\nF(0)&=- \\frac{4 \\left(0\\right)^{3}}{3} - 3 \\left(0\\right)^{2} - \\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=F(1)-F(0) \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{16}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{16}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721947 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The factor $y\\prime(t)$ is missing." :answer/id #uuid "2107a1b5-c106-51b4-8047-53eb9412829b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(- 8 \\sin{t} + 6 \\cos{t} + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721942} {:answer/feedback "The signed $y$ derivative has been negated." :answer/id #uuid "4d9e89d3-1c4c-59b1-a7d3-2770f1916b72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(- 8 \\sin{t} + 6 \\cos{t} + 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721949} {:answer/feedback "This expression uses the specified path, substituted function, and signed $y$ derivative." :answer/id #uuid "5135573b-74be-5336-917e-b91c31891567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(- 8 \\sin{t} + 6 \\cos{t} + 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721950} {:answer/feedback "This uses $x\\prime(t)$ in place of $y\\prime(t)$." :answer/id #uuid "c1a20810-9804-5fa7-b275-c032f3334722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(- 8 \\sin{t} + 6 \\cos{t} + 1\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721964} {:answer/feedback "This uses the $y$ coordinate itself instead of its derivative." :answer/id #uuid "c38f93be-eefe-5d12-821f-0c45ee5eea60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(- 8 \\sin{t} + 6 \\cos{t} + 1\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721966}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721950} :answer-field/id #uuid "22183441-f10c-5661-924c-d2749bd755f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3e5f3c20-fa33-53c4-b7a5-53ea7bc613be" :question/problem "![Directed path C](images/e8/e889899407c1daa89187078eedc63e91e17c9cb6e4393e74a52c1de69af505e4.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(2 x - 2 y + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is one quarter of the ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{9}+\\frac{y^2}{16}=1$, directed counterclockwise from $A=(0,-4)$ to $B=(3,0)$, as shown above? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 \\cos{t},\\,4 \\sin{t}\\rangle$.*" :question/worked-solution "For a parametrization following the directed path,\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\\int_a^b f(x(t),y(t))\\,y\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nChoose\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 \\cos{t},\\,4 \\sin{t}\\rangle,\\qquad \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\le t\\le 2 \\pi.\n$$\n\nThe squared coordinate ratios sum to $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, so this parametrization lies on the curve. It travels counterclockwise. The endpoints occur at $t=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and $t=2 \\pi$; the interval covers the specified portion once.\n\nThe signed differential factor is\n\n$$\ny\\prime(t)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(4 \\sin{t}\\right)=4 \\cos{t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting both coordinates into the given function gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x(t),y(t))&=\\left.\\left(2 x - 2 y + 1\\right)\\right|_{x=3 \\cos{t},\\,y=4 \\sin{t}}\\\\&=- 8 \\sin{t} + 6 \\cos{t} + 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, retaining the signed derivative,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\&\\quad=4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(- 8 \\sin{t} + 6 \\cos{t} + 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721954 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The factor $y\\prime(t)$ is missing." :answer/id #uuid "1a31b993-1472-5fbc-8fcc-ebbaaf7c6694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi}\\left(16 - 16 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721941} {:answer/feedback "This uses the $y$ coordinate itself instead of its derivative." :answer/id #uuid "4950ccf8-a579-5bb5-a7c1-ab33c9060ee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi}\\left(16 - 16 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721948} {:answer/feedback "The scale of the $y$ coordinate was lost when differentiating." :answer/id #uuid "6488fb63-f746-5a95-beeb-57a6e5dcb250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi}\\left(16 - 16 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721955} {:answer/feedback "This expression uses the specified path, substituted function, and signed $y$ derivative." :answer/id #uuid "96cbe9d5-490f-5bf7-9252-1a9df6ac6121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi}\\left(16 - 16 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721958} {:answer/feedback "This uses $x\\prime(t)$ in place of $y\\prime(t)$." :answer/id #uuid "d3cfff77-d4a5-5eaa-9d5c-9725903aead3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi}\\left(16 - 16 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721969}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721958} :answer-field/id #uuid "2507754d-045d-5e86-a0ed-11c7886afac7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5d15d031-1d8c-5c1a-8df0-dd3ac1647ab4" :question/problem "![Directed path C](images/49/4938a35678aa2d7d815af2165204560a743aac43dba7a956b80cf6b61725983e.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(16 - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is three quarters of the ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{16}+\\frac{y^2}{16}=1$, directed counterclockwise from $A=(0,-4)$ to $B=(-4,0)$, as shown above? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 4 \\cos{t},\\,4 \\sin{t}\\rangle$.*" :question/worked-solution "For a parametrization following the directed path,\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\\int_a^b f(x(t),y(t))\\,y\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nChoose\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 4 \\cos{t},\\,4 \\sin{t}\\rangle,\\qquad \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\le t\\le 3 \\pi.\n$$\n\nThe squared coordinate ratios sum to $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, so this parametrization lies on the curve. It travels counterclockwise. The endpoints occur at $t=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and $t=3 \\pi$; the interval covers the specified portion once.\n\nThe signed differential factor is\n\n$$\ny\\prime(t)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(4 \\sin{t}\\right)=4 \\cos{t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting both coordinates into the given function gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x(t),y(t))&=\\left.\\left(16 - y^{2}\\right)\\right|_{x=4 \\cos{t},\\,y=4 \\sin{t}}\\\\&=16 - 16 \\sin^{2}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, retaining the signed derivative,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\&\\quad=4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi}\\left(16 - 16 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721959 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The signed $y$ derivative has been negated." :answer/id #uuid "017a70b7-ed55-51f8-a295-0eacc3e4e79e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(9 t^{2} + 12 t + 4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721940} {:answer/feedback "The factor $y\\prime(t)$ is missing." :answer/id #uuid "35042666-7fe0-58ad-99d9-1b9f7563a0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(9 t^{2} + 12 t + 4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721946} {:answer/feedback "This expression uses the specified path, substituted function, and signed $y$ derivative." :answer/id #uuid "c818209b-35fa-5e4a-b6da-7b5edbe6f2c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(9 t^{2} + 12 t + 4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721967} {:answer/feedback "This uses $x\\prime(t)$ in place of $y\\prime(t)$." :answer/id #uuid "e7c2fd25-2df7-54af-be39-1e5dc8cb0d26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(9 t^{2} + 12 t + 4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721971} {:answer/feedback "The signed displacement magnitude was replaced by one in the differential." :answer/id #uuid "f1ed1885-bfb8-569f-8be7-6a704b79ca90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(9 t^{2} + 12 t + 4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721973}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721967} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0f88568-94c7-5c56-8005-eaa6c8270f28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a6a997fe-01bc-5605-bdbb-569549c18d80" :question/problem "![Directed path C](images/42/427a5f3f2ceb974bb7196b7f393252366e9a8cfbd1e1956d7d6286aa86339938.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=(2,-2)$ to $B=(5,-4)$, as shown above? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 t + 2,\\,- 2 t - 2\\rangle$.*" :question/worked-solution "For a parametrization following the directed path,\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\\int_a^b f(x(t),y(t))\\,y\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nChoose\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 t + 2,\\,- 2 t - 2\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThe segment parametrization gives $\\mathbf r(0)=(2,-2)$ and $\\mathbf r(1)=(5,-4)$, so it follows the specified direction.\n\nThe signed differential factor is\n\n$$\ny\\prime(t)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 t - 2\\right)=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting both coordinates into the given function gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x(t),y(t))&=\\left.\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right|_{x=3 t + 2,\\,y=- 2 t - 2}\\\\&=9 t^{2} + 12 t + 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, retaining the signed derivative,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\&\\quad=-2\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(9 t^{2} + 12 t + 4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This uses $x\\prime(t)$ in place of $y\\prime(t)$." :answer/id #uuid "34588be4-b979-51b8-b9bd-47a98cb2d12d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\left(16 \\sin^{2}{t} + \\cos^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721945} {:answer/feedback "The signed $y$ derivative has been negated." :answer/id #uuid "58083801-8857-59f0-8d3c-995bd5d4d925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\left(16 \\sin^{2}{t} + \\cos^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721953} {:answer/feedback "The factor $y\\prime(t)$ is missing." :answer/id #uuid "65f7cfa9-2afc-553a-8ebd-4513293b78cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :a