\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722016} {:answer/feedback "This expression uses the specified path, substituted function, and signed $y$ derivative." :answer/id #uuid "935de39d-e522-5fa0-bee5-6281e264eec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left(4 \\sin{t} - 8 \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722019} {:answer/feedback "The factor $y\\prime(t)$ is missing." :answer/id #uuid "da07c961-b0ef-5595-8940-6f506314ac09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left(4 \\sin{t} - 8 \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722019} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eaa2491-57ea-5b08-a9df-a34c2b8383c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8b265f5c-7a94-55c2-a4f6-4b332278faf1" :question/problem "![Directed path C](images/c6/c6651e5c78464bb97e274f5133362e7754902513683535f3ae6b4334808d1153.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(- 2 x + 2 y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is one half of the ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{16}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1$, directed counterclockwise from $A=(-4,0)$ to $B=(4,0)$, as shown above? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "For a parametrization following the directed path,\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\\int_a^b f(x(t),y(t))\\,y\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nChoose\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 4 \\cos{t},\\,2 \\sin{t}\\rangle,\\qquad \\pi\\le t\\le 2 \\pi.\n$$\n\nThe squared coordinate ratios sum to $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, so this parametrization lies on the curve. It travels counterclockwise. The endpoints occur at $t=\\pi$ and $t=2 \\pi$; the interval covers the specified portion once.\n\nThe signed differential factor is\n\n$$\ny\\prime(t)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 \\sin{t}\\right)=2 \\cos{t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting both coordinates into the given function gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x(t),y(t))&=\\left.\\left(- 2 x + 2 y - 1\\right)\\right|_{x=4 \\cos{t},\\,y=2 \\sin{t}}\\\\&=4 \\sin{t} - 8 \\cos{t} - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, retaining the signed derivative,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\&\\quad=2\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left(4 \\sin{t} - 8 \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This uses $x\\prime(t)$ in place of $y\\prime(t)$." :answer/id #uuid "3ee24257-b9f9-56f4-b4be-8d08070eebe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\left(- 6 \\sin{t} + \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722010} {:answer/feedback "The sign of the $x$ coordinate was changed in the substitution." :answer/id #uuid "928e7e63-01e3-52e3-86a6-de92348d37f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\left(- 6 \\sin{t} - \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722018} {:answer/feedback "This expression uses the specified path, substituted function, and signed $y$ derivative." :answer/id #uuid "a2139c40-4e36-5dac-aa82-bdb8082f03c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\left(- 6 \\sin{t} + \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722021} {:answer/feedback "The coordinates have been interchanged in the substitution into $f$." :answer/id #uuid "e141eaec-9f2e-50a5-8776-0dbc8a5b73c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\left(3 \\sin{t} - 2 \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722027} {:answer/feedback "The factor $y\\prime(t)$ is missing." :answer/id #uuid "e89b87f2-68ac-5d14-93fc-01540ee31dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\left(- 6 \\sin{t} + \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722030}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722021} :answer-field/id #uuid "e85a615d-2cb2-5544-ae0a-364efdf08d73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c70aad24-80b3-5f17-9fc9-cbd924d3a280" :question/problem "![Directed path C](images/f3/f395c91bd726bb62a450b0403865283d6a8425ab2d58fc73328c1a1c98211964.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(x - 2 y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is one half of the ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{1}+\\frac{y^2}{9}=1$, directed counterclockwise from $A=(0,3)$ to $B=(0,-3)$, as shown above? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "For a parametrization following the directed path,\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\\int_a^b f(x(t),y(t))\\,y\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nChoose\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle \\cos{t},\\,3 \\sin{t}\\rangle,\\qquad \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le t\\le \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squared coordinate ratios sum to $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, so this parametrization lies on the curve. It travels counterclockwise. The endpoints occur at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $t=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$; the interval covers the specified portion once.\n\nThe signed differential factor is\n\n$$\ny\\prime(t)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(3 \\sin{t}\\right)=3 \\cos{t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting both coordinates into the given function gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x(t),y(t))&=\\left.\\left(x - 2 y - 1\\right)\\right|_{x=\\cos{t},\\,y=3 \\sin{t}}\\\\&=- 6 \\sin{t} + \\cos{t} - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, retaining the signed derivative,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\&\\quad=3\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}\\left(- 6 \\sin{t} + \\cos{t} - 1\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The signed $y$ derivative has been negated." :answer/id #uuid "01095bfa-39a1-5fc6-877f-b99b9c6eee1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(9 \\sin^{2}{t} + \\cos^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722004} {:answer/feedback "This uses the $y$ coordinate itself instead of its derivative." :answer/id #uuid "452a5072-94f2-586e-8028-3ce0c3f27f52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(9 \\sin^{2}{t} + \\cos^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722011} {:answer/feedback "The differential factor is squared instead of used once." :answer/id #uuid "6a031ace-e600-5dd5-a7d4-ee9b67e2c600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(9 \\sin^{2}{t} + \\cos^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos^{2}{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722013} {:answer/feedback "This uses $x\\prime(t)$ in place of $y\\prime(t)$." :answer/id #uuid "6d0ead34-e3b2-52d2-b097-2a78c03a7796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(9 \\sin^{2}{t} + \\cos^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722014} {:answer/feedback "This expression uses the specified path, substituted function, and signed $y$ derivative." :answer/id #uuid "da9c25b1-197c-52f6-bc62-2b8d6f77e1d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\in