ight)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This expression uses the specified path, substituted function, and signed $y$ derivative." :answer/id #uuid "28155bc4-f647-5c19-910d-78b0e56f5f4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}}\\left(4 - 4 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722007} {:answer/feedback "This uses $x\\prime(t)$ in place of $y\\prime(t)$." :answer/id #uuid "2c869237-e080-5a35-8ed7-4025f2f10ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}}\\left(4 - 4 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\sin{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722008} {:answer/feedback "The squared coordinate was used to the first power." :answer/id #uuid "a1186f49-2134-5493-af49-02afaf3db198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}}\\left(4 - 2 \\sin{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722020} {:answer/feedback "The factor $y\\prime(t)$ is missing." :answer/id #uuid "ae992042-00f5-56d7-b8a5-a4641ca7f1e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}}\\left(4 - 4 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722022} {:answer/feedback "The coordinates have been interchanged in the substitution into $f$." :answer/id #uuid "ee2555bd-5770-5bba-ae88-4524cd93a283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}}\\left(4 - 16 \\cos^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722007} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cd587f8-049b-5a9d-b7f9-3801c1bdb30f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e396285c-5024-5811-9b3a-80c1436f1b7a" :question/problem "![Directed path C](images/81/81ceb436a8c1dc03537d69d51dcadf2eeeb5ee382f1bcc9696e34aa5d42bb161.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(4 - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is one half of the ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{16}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1$, directed counterclockwise from $A=(0,-2)$ to $B=(0,2)$, as shown above? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "For a parametrization following the directed path,\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\\int_a^b f(x(t),y(t))\\,y\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nChoose\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 4 \\cos{t},\\,2 \\sin{t}\\rangle,\\qquad \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\le t\\le \\frac{5 \\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squared coordinate ratios sum to $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, so this parametrization lies on the curve. It travels counterclockwise. The endpoints occur at $t=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and $t=\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}$; the interval covers the specified portion once.\n\nThe signed differential factor is\n\n$$\ny\\prime(t)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 \\sin{t}\\right)=2 \\cos{t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting both coordinates into the given function gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x(t),y(t))&=\\left.\\left(4 - y^{2}\\right)\\right|_{x=4 \\cos{t},\\,y=2 \\sin{t}}\\\\&=4 - 4 \\sin^{2}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, retaining the signed derivative,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\&\\quad=2\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}}\\left(4 - 4 \\sin^{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\cos{t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722053 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e91e45d-c21c-5ca1-abec-1a6b81c8f0ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722063} {:answer/id #uuid "861d5e5d-b164-56de-870e-32986f2d831a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722068} {:answer/id #uuid "97395662-b225-54e6-b185-5e70ecb651ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722070} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4bb0f8-93c1-5c17-a06d-6f62749718d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722079} {:answer/id #uuid "f34163e6-10a3-5f14-adaa-3316e745a929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722085}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722068} :answer-field/id #uuid "bce8a310-ffcb-5c16-a83c-8fff1197e59b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1312b275-cc74-5b75-8dea-a645bdff1d43" :question/problem "![](images/14/140df7664edfa54f0af250561876700abdc3fec016b916cdf463925660a3806b.png)\n\nEvaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(x + \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=\\left(3,\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$ to $B=\\left(2,0\\right)$, as shown." :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the requested integral. The path can be parameterized by\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 - t,\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{t}{2}\\rangle.\n$$\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ at $A$ to $t=1$ at $B$. Use the signed coordinate derivative $y'(t)=- \\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=- t + \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{t}{2}\\right) \\right)} + 3\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- t + \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{t}{2}\\right) \\right)} + 3\\right)\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{2} - \\frac{\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{t}{2}\\right) \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nFor the trigonometric term, the argument derivative is $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{t}{2}\\right)\\right)=- \\frac{\\pi}{2}$. Keep that argument when applying the sine or cosine primitive.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{2} - \\frac{\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{t}{2}\\right) \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{t^{2}}{4} - \\frac{3 t}{2} + \\sin{\\left(\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{t}{2}\\right) \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{5}{4}\\right)-\\left(1\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{9}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n The differential is $\\mathrm{d}y$, so an arc-length speed factor is not used."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c2eb182-6f84-5101-8fd9-41b044fa9edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722059} {:answer/id #uuid "5d3a89ed-5bcc-5273-bde9-e6f4f655dc40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722060} {:answer/id #uuid "85b20aa5-ea44-5ce1-ba9b-83a441069141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722067} {:answer/id #uuid "ce65159a-67ac-5933-9fe2-3a829363dfe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722081} {:answer/id #uuid "e009e0a3-767e-5e47-8d54-8d315e214ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722083}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722081} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc42d1b4-bd77-5494-a137-902f1ae87da0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "72f107c5-efbb-557a-91dd-4e358f3b7171" :question/problem "![](images/61/61c87cca35f6e0319e2b4e056e505df7795e574983d9c993e1d96182c6c57fe6.png)\n\nEvaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(\\sqrt{x} + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=\\left(1,-1\\right)$ to $B=\\left(0,0\\right)$, as shown." :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the requested integral. The path can be parameterized by\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 1 - t,t - 1\\rangle.\n$$\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ at $A$ to $t=1$ at $B$. Use the signed coordinate derivative $y'(t)=1$.\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=2 t + \\sqrt{1 - t} - 2\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t + \\sqrt{1 - t} - 2\\right)\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}2 t + \\sqrt{1 - t} - 2\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}2 t + \\sqrt{1 - t} - 2\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[t^{2} - 2 t - \\frac{2 \\left(1 - t\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(-1\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{1}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n The differential is $\\mathrm{d}y$, so an arc-length speed factor is not used."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0620d7e5-eea3-54c9-84d7-b43e573d9017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722052} {:answer/id #uuid "1bb09b12-ae9c-5b38-927d-8c7fd1ce5f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722054} {:answer/id #uuid "b2399d19-2d0d-5b30-b415-5239bfef20f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722074} {:answer/id #uuid "bdbbe1d4-6783-511e-b930-3891f129a997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722077} {:answer/id #uuid "c52d324c-e38f-518a-89b3-fe4b3ea36313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722078}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722077} :answer-field/id #uuid "d53babbc-7fe5-5b2e-9b7f-3e9c1d0c6602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "818241c2-14e6-5fbd-8dee-aeb7578df607" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b513d1fd9777406080e133fd9bd62ddce5f14380603498717b001723d011a38.png)\n\nEvaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(x^{2} + \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi y}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=\\left(-2,2\\right)$ to $B=\\left(-2,0\\right)$, as shown." :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the requested integral. The path can be parameterized by\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle -2,2 - 2 t\\rangle.\n$$\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ at $A$ to $t=1$ at $B$. Use the signed coordinate derivative $y'(t)=-2$.\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=\\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi \\left(1 - t\\right) \\right)} + 4\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi \\left(1 - t\\right) \\right)} + 4\\right)\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}- 2 \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi \\left(1 - t\\right) \\right)} - 8\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nFor the trigonometric term, the argument derivative is $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(\\pi \\left(1 - t\\right)\\right)=- \\pi$. Keep that argument when applying the sine or cosine primitive.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}- 2 \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi \\left(1 - t\\right) \\right)} - 8\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[- 8 t - 2 \\cos{\\left(\\pi \\left(1 - t\\right) \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(-10\\right)-\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n&=-12.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n The differential is $\\mathrm{d}y$, so an arc-length speed factor is not used."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02272baa-3c9d-520a-bbd2-52f2052a2591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722051} {:answer/id #uuid "323d02ef-2a1b-5b89-abc7-9dc207441bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722056} {:answer/id #uuid "39a0d9f7-7cac-5b28-a7bb-fff6a0875607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722058} {:answer/id #uuid "79e0e0ea-042e-55ac-bd0a-da886340aa14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722065} {:answer/id #uuid "e4561376-effa-5510-bd27-3b75cb6f5f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722084}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722065} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc665cff-f9f8-5167-9677-bbb70a1416ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a246ba1b-70a2-5bba-af7e-d5b14c02f65f" :question/problem "![](images/93/93ba377ef875077d46f17d69570028d5af7d006edce29832037292554603b074.png)\n\nEvaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(- 2 x + \\sqrt{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=\\left(2,1\\right)$ to $B=\\left(0,0\\right)$, as shown." :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the requested integral. The path can be parameterized by\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 2 - 2 t,1 - t\\rangle.\n$$\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ at $A$ to $t=1$ at $B$. Use the signed coordinate derivative $y'(t)=-1$.\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=4 t + \\sqrt{1 - t} - 4\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 t + \\sqrt{1 - t} - 4\\right)\\left(-1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}- 4 t - \\sqrt{1 - t} + 4\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}- 4 t - \\sqrt{1 - t} + 4\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[- 2 t^{2} + 4 t + \\frac{2 \\left(1 - t\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(2\\right)-\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{4}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n The differential is $\\mathrm{d}y$, so an arc-length speed factor is not used."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23946629-f272-59ee-b4f0-09bb69591e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722055} {:answer/id #uuid "3935d1b9-c0b7-54f3-b268-3da4be80fea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722057} {:answer/id #uuid "679ad227-10ed-5201-9a78-e6df2987c48f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722061} {:answer/id #uuid "8c325570-fb05-5974-84b7-31461baa7826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722069} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b617bd-4fb9-5bf9-9288-6810c4c87261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722073}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722073} :answer-field/id #uuid "6deda1dc-8eba-589d-97ce-f09a0b103b47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a250a17b-f9d4-5383-a1f3-15c95ab84fda" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d416375ad6b2bccb5cfd28d929d06c42d64dca25dbfb3e21af0384b17a0c7a7e.png)\n\nEvaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(2 x + 2 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=\\left(3,1\\right)$ to $B=\\left(1,0\\right)$, as shown." :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the requested integral. The path can be parameterized by\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 - 2 t,1 - t\\rangle.\n$$\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ at $A$ to $t=1$ at $B$. Use the signed coordinate derivative $y'(t)=-1$.\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=- 4 t + 2 \\left(1 - t\\right)^{2} + 6\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 4 t + 2 \\left(1 - t\\right)^{2} + 6\\right)\\left(-1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}4 t - 2 \\left(1 - t\\right)^{2} - 6\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}4 t - 2 \\left(1 - t\\right)^{2} - 6\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[- \\frac{2 t^{3}}{3} + 4 t^{2} - 8 t\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{14}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{14}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n The differential is $\\mathrm{d}y$, so an arc-length speed factor is not used."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb3a874-0c1e-5707-ab7a-9e87702f7e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722098} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff7e7b5-637a-54e9-a291-cf47cda34acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} - 8 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 32 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722103} {:answer/id #uuid "6a036f6c-8852-5e4e-9ff3-205f5639c1a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{4}} - 8 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 32 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722105} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ffe7fd-f47b-57c2-abac-7b15f44611ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 8 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722114} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d39116-aee8-5181-8878-289391b25b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} - 16 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 16 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722118} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a37adf0-6f20-572d-93bd-93887bfb3e13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "271e3484-b755-5dd7-be14-2159ca5795e0" :question/problem "![Oriented path](images/df/df948e65c856771e0497693fa9bc6f941ec68ee0e1fc19ce941d7ae2c0658153.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C x + 2 y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the arc of $\\frac{x^2}{16}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1$, traversed counterclockwise through one quarter of the ellipse from $(-4,0)$ to $(0,-2)$, as shown? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n*Hint: Use $\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle$.*" :question/worked-solution "The coordinate scales follow from $\\frac{x^2}{16}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1$. Choose the parametrization below. Increasing the parameter follows the stated counterclockwise direction. The parameter starts at $\\pi$ and ends at $\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$, giving the required endpoints.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle,\\qquad \\pi\\le t\\le \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates, then differentiate the first coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+2(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&=4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\ x\\prime(t)&=- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the two factors, keeping the signed derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)&=(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&=- 16 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 16 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse this density with the oriented parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C x + 2 y\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} - 16 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 16 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d7fa55-500b-589c-aba5-397edbfe7ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1} - t^{2} - 4\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722087} {:answer/id #uuid "2451f179-eea9-5788-a2da-0b63c0ee6280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1} t^{2} + 4\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722090} {:answer/id #uuid "494f874d-af99-55bf-b8d2-945a48e69221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1} - 4 t^{2} - 16\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722096} {:answer/id #uuid "6986f2fb-8eb5-5d06-8f63-df32263eaebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1} - 64 t^{2} + 4 t + 8\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722104} {:answer/id #uuid "ef90e0e2-77e0-5205-be54-bc62dae522c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1} 4 t^{2} + 16\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722120}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722096} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f965823-fea2-5853-a0cd-7a6d407f7198" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "54f7e125-909f-5a1e-8ac9-809833f7da33" :question/problem "![Oriented path](images/ef/ef0becba15edb6e9745e6fd36a919a018223e5b2d1e015dac806dcbafadcae8b.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C x + y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment traversed from $(0,-2)$ to $(-4,-3)$, as shown? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n*Hint: Use $\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle - 4 t,- t - 2\\rangle$.*" :question/worked-solution "Interpolate from the initial point to the terminal point. The parameter starts at $0$ and ends at $1$, giving the required endpoints.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle - 4 t,- t - 2\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 1\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates, then differentiate the first coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(- 4 t)+(- t - 2)^{2}\\\\&=t^{2} + 4,\\\\ x\\prime(t)&=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the two factors, keeping the signed derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)&=(t^{2} + 4)(-4)\\\\&=- 4 t^{2} - 16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse this density with the oriented parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C x + y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\int_{0}^{1} f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1} - 4 t^{2} - 16\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24a1c1a0-2862-59aa-af27-2e65e1e0a2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722091} {:answer/id #uuid "534f361f-b840-5239-8e61-b881e8eec646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722099} {:answer/id #uuid "8aacab06-be1f-54e2-b391-3adc41244193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722108} {:answer/id #uuid "9c3c0ff8-fecd-5b65-bc8c-478e274f0fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722110} {:answer/id #uuid "cf1a6fba-d9a5-5241-ad7c-d91d8f28e8a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722091} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e5b5c1-0f7e-53b1-828d-86652d0fc30f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f93b9de-fb07-5a4d-b4c6-1378da7c482b" :question/problem "![Oriented path](images/f7/f779ac496d7e931e0db1aa172e0901d144a236a44934de69c5223b707f3b5ee3.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the arc of $\\frac{x^2}{1}+\\frac{y^2}{16}=1$, traversed clockwise through one quarter of the ellipse from $(1,0)$ to $(0,-4)$, as shown? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n*Hint: Use $\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle$.*" :question/worked-solution "The coordinate scales follow from $\\frac{x^2}{1}+\\frac{y^2}{16}=1$. Choose the parametrization below. Increasing the parameter follows the stated clockwise direction. The parameter starts at $0$ and ends at $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, giving the required endpoints.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates, then differentiate the first coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f(\\mathbf r(t))&=1(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&=- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\ x\\prime(t)&=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the two factors, keeping the signed derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)&=(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&=4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse this density with the oriented parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C y\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d690255-939f-55a2-a5f4-79a09ca19638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi} - 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722089} {:answer/id #uuid "2b739601-5149-5e53-833b-ac82ab74ef49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi} 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722093} {:answer/id #uuid "5d860913-cffd-5a83-88b6-2c7693aa458a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi} 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722101} {:answer/id #uuid "9255fbe7-17f8-5466-a6e2-9ad0d8c8b6bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{9 \\pi}{4}} 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722109} {:answer/id #uuid "e75c9c7e-8e4f-5f61-a5c2-bc62495bd9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi} 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722119}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722101} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d9474db-3b05-5538-aefe-758c44c128e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b0ce803b-65fe-51fa-8348-4ba45273bdc8" :question/problem "![Oriented path](images/de/def37b214cf1509774a63a8fe9c2e33b4ac2ee5225ddbccfa47794e08f01c5eb.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C x + 2 y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the arc of $\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{y^2}{1}=1$, traversed clockwise through three quarters of the ellipse from $(0,1)$ to $(-2,0)$, as shown? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n*Hint: Use $\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle$.*" :question/worked-solution "The coordinate scales follow from $\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{y^2}{1}=1$. Choose the parametrization below. Increasing the parameter follows the stated clockwise direction. The parameter starts at $\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and ends at $3 \\pi$, giving the required endpoints.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle,\\qquad \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\le t\\le 3 \\pi\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates, then differentiate the first coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+2(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\ x\\prime(t)&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the two factors, keeping the signed derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)&=(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&=4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse this density with the oriented parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C x + 2 y\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi} f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{3 \\pi} 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722121 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c72dc5d-955d-5628-9a7c-8be9d39c717e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}} 256 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{3}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722088} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb4f45a-8308-52e2-ab0e-78fcd5a8d8f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722094} {:answer/id #uuid "ab33adb5-65ec-564b-beaf-b285c25e552e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} 256 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722112} {:answer/id #uuid "cb68f71d-edd6-5340-a587-597993e05606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} - 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722115} {:answer/id #uuid "d26cf420-4e4c-55c2-bba8-c699e90efaf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} - 256 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722117}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722117} :answer-field/id #uuid "746fc3eb-1cfb-5bc1-962b-48283eef62d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fb13de21-830f-56e7-9383-b2ef6e314a29" :question/problem "![Oriented path](images/f6/f6a6a19c5ccbd0b00fcc16e4dd1a06814749f69405182162ea4943439faf5b5d.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C x^{2} y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the arc of $x^2+y^2=16$, traversed counterclockwise through one quarter of the circle from $(0,-4)$ to $(4,0)$, as shown? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n*Hint: Use $\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle$.*" :question/worked-solution "The coordinate scales follow from $x^2+y^2=16$. Choose the parametrization below. Increasing the parameter follows the stated counterclockwise direction. The parameter starts at $\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and ends at $2 \\pi$, giving the required endpoints.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle,\\qquad \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\le t\\le 2 \\pi\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates, then differentiate the first coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^{2}(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&=64 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\ x\\prime(t)&=- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the two factors, keeping the signed derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)&=(64 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)})(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&=- 256 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse this density with the oriented parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C x^{2} y\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} f(\\mathbf r(t))x\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} - 256 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62bf3ec4-5443-5941-a273-066c80f8d3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722134} {:answer/id #uuid "9aad4b81-01db-592f-8376-ffe4b0e41d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722136} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0ed7d1-da9d-53fa-ac1d-bb9160a90f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722142} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa1d9e8-68b3-5d27-bbaa-b8b812b7f051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722148} {:answer/id #uuid "f48d2206-3929-51de-abb6-6ba53c0282ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722148} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d21c3c8-34d7-5946-843a-f23d9e69dba8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722128}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "05aa996b-12f7-54df-9d7f-cf87f9385e38" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3e96f4817f69f22f82be668496ce0b17b4196f70af8a1750924c3b5bda0fe006.png)\n\nEvaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(2 x - 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=\\left(0,0\\right)$ to $B=\\left(-1,-2\\right)$, as shown." :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the requested integral. The path can be parameterized by\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle - t,- 2 t\\rangle.\n$$\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ at $A$ to $t=1$ at $B$. Use the signed coordinate derivative $y'(t)=-2$.\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=2 t\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t\\right)\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}- 4 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}- 4 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[- 2 t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(-2\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n The differential is $\\mathrm{d}y$, so an arc-length speed factor is not used."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "369e2cae-8ba9-5ce4-8268-85632577e2f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722131} {:answer/id #uuid "9c860431-464b-578a-9b26-d0bbb61a0062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722137} {:answer/id #uuid "9faf6212-adee-540f-940a-056bf50cb7b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722138} {:answer/id #uuid "bad0d338-258f-5cd2-818a-65797709e8bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722141} {:answer/id #uuid "edbc5afa-6b53-5ef9-9c02-4234b91fbd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722149}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722149} :answer-field/id #uuid "50defe84-6ae2-50b6-b546-f9a6e63114fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1eff3e82-0451-50f5-863f-bf409ceffa78" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e3d2c8cfb30b17a72254cc17f29ce88a1921a1358981c09f726bf06395308789.png)\n\nEvaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(2 x - 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=\\left(2,3\\right)$ to $B=\\left(0,2\\right)$, as shown." :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the requested integral. The path can be parameterized by\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 2 - 2 t,3 - t\\rangle.\n$$\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ at $A$ to $t=1$ at $B$. Use the signed coordinate derivative $y'(t)=-1$.\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=- 2 t - 2\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 2 t - 2\\right)\\left(-1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}2 t + 2\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}2 t + 2\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[t^{2} + 2 t\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(3\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n The differential is $\\mathrm{d}y$, so an arc-length speed factor is not used."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c815ba1-7d9e-5019-86f2-6bbd342e669a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722124} {:answer/id #uuid "29377790-a9e5-52ab-9f6e-2ffb6cdf0ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722130} {:answer/id #uuid "4480bf47-ccf8-5bdc-acf7-0eece7d60e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722132} {:answer/id #uuid "b07a2048-76da-5e36-9c0f-6fe98d69d6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722139} {:answer/id #uuid "dd38dfe9-7038-5ce6-8436-76a7b255e7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722132} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c8f50f0-7dae-53bf-82d1-5f8072afa1c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d828d0bb-daa2-5978-99d6-72b7d7c25a56" :question/problem "![](images/73/736c4db27d66b2ca39e24b91abdc42df8ae71749c4e99daf509414c7ef402d82.png)\n\nEvaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\left(x - 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the line segment directed from $A=\\left(-5,3\\right)$ to $B=\\left(-2,0\\right)$, as shown." :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the requested integral. The path can be parameterized by\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 t - 5,3 - 3 t\\rangle.\n$$\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ at $A$ to $t=1$ at $B$. Use the signed coordinate derivative $y'(t)=-3$.\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=9 t - 11\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(9 t - 11\\right)\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{1}33 - 27 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\int_{0}^{1}33 - 27 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[- \\frac{27 t^{2}}{2} + 33 t\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{39}{2}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{39}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n The differential is $\\mathrm{d}y$, so an arc-length speed factor is not used."}]}
